==English==

===Adjective===
{{infl|en|adjective|head=[[all over]] [[the]] [[place]]}}
# {{idiom}} [[inconsistent|Inconsistent]]; lacking a clear [[pattern]].
#: ''I asked each person in turn, and their answers were '''all over the place'''.''

===Preposition===
{{infl|en|preposition|head=[[all over]] [[the]] [[place]]}}

# {{literally}} [[covering|Covering]] a [[location]] [[thoroughly]] or [[completely]].
#: When the house caught on fire the firemen came and sprayed water '''all over the place'''.
# {{idiom}} ''(of an [[accidental]] [[spill]])'' In a [[random]] way; creating a [[substantial]] [[mess]].
#: ''I dropped my glass and milk went '''all over the place'''.''
#: ''The cart fell over and there were apples '''all over the place'''.''


